0,Music of Papua New Guinea - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Papua_New_Guinea,"The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life.","Kanum, Bädi",South-Central Papuan
1,Kanum people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanum_people,"Kanum people (Kanume) are an ethnic group that inhabit the border area of Merauke Regency in South Papua and Western Province in Papua New Guinea. The Kanum are considered a subgroup of the Marind, but they have their own language, Kanum, that belongs to the Yam language family.","Kanum, Bädi",South-Central Papuan
2,"Kanum, Bädi Language (KHD) - L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/khd/,"Bädi Kanum is an endangered indigenous language of Indonesia. It belongs to the South-Central Papuan language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by the elderly only. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Kanum, Bädi",South-Central Papuan
